{
  "id": "28293_hakaru",
  "headword": "{量|はか}る",
  "reading": "はかる",
  "romaji": "hakaru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to weigh; to measure (volume or weight)",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to weigh; to measure (weight or volume)",
      "explanation": "To measure how much something weighs or its volume, typically using a scale or measuring vessel."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "28293_hakaru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{体重|たいじゅう}を{量|はか}る。",
      "english": "To weigh oneself.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28293_hakaru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{砂糖|さとう}を{百|ひゃく}グラム{量|はか}った。",
      "english": "I measured out 100 grams of sugar.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28293_hakaru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{宅配便|たくはいびん}に{出|だ}す{前|まえ}に、{荷物|にもつ}の{重|おも}さを{量|はか}っておく。",
      "english": "Weigh the package before sending it by parcel delivery.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28293_hakaru_ex4",
      "japanese": "{米|こめ}をカップで{量|はか}って{炊|た}いた。",
      "english": "I measured the rice with a cup and cooked it.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Kanji variant of はかる reserved for weight and volume. For length, depth, or speed use {測|はか}る; for time or set-phrase 'planning' use {計|はか}る.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {体重|たいじゅう}を{量|はか}る: to weigh oneself\n- {重|おも}さを{量|はか}る: to measure the weight\n- {分量|ぶんりょう}を{量|はか}る: to measure out a quantity\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {測|はか}る: to measure length, depth, height, speed\n- {計|はか}る: to measure time; to plan",
